{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013dn1NsFCUSzxrjffHALxvn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n6\t- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 2-3x (median across configurations), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; when naive bias is near zero, global correction creates bias where none existed. For the difference-in-means estimator, the amplification magnitude does NOT monotonically increase with K (K=2 extreme: up to 2.86× vs K=4 extreme: up to 2.41×); however, with nonlinear estimators such as CausalForest, more subgroups amplify the effect substantially (K=4/extreme: up to 5.9×) due to compounding estimation noise in tree-based CATE. Global correction increases subgroup-level bias in ~50% of the parameter space.\n11\t\n12\t2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) substantially reduces subgroup-level bias when misclassification heterogeneity is sufficiently high, while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. HB provides meaningful RMSE reduction by borrowing strength across groups (classic James-Stein shrinkage). We provide precise crossover thresholds: EC-HTE outperforms global correction in RMSE with as few as 250 expert labels (K=2, high heterogeneity), scaling to ~1000 for K=4. **Boundary condition**: when expert labels per subgroup < ~25, shrinkage can be harmful — stratified MLE is preferred. **EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed — the diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) identifies these scenarios.** **CONFIRMED** by exp-003 full 100 MC (1200 runs, 0 errors). HB crossover at ~11 experts/subgroup; ≥25 recommended for robust performance. Demonstrated with both difference-in-means and CausalForestDML (exp-011: consistent bias reduction pattern, ec_hte_forest |bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16). CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect (up to 5.9x in K=4/extreme) due to nonlinear CATE estimation.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic that simultaneously predicts when global correction is harmful (Claim 1) and when the expert label investment for stratified correction is worthwhile (connecting to the budget guidelines from Claim 2). This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE — even without adopting EC-HTE, knowing when global correction backfires is practically actionable.\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis across computational social science (CSS) — e.g., sentiment framing moderates message effectiveness, hate speech type moderates intervention impact. LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education; documented across CSS tasks including sentiment, stance, toxicity). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic CSS benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x (median), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels. Combined with PPCI, the composition achieves near-zero bias (0.005) even when both covariate and outcome errors are present.\"\n25\t\n26\t- **Oracle framing**: When reporting DGP C results where ec_hte_ppci outperforms oracle, always use \"covariate-oracle\" (true Z + observed Y), never unqualified \"oracle\". Frame as \"composite correction is necessary and sufficient when both error types coexist\" — NOT \"beats oracle\". The result is by construction (ec_hte_ppci corrects both error types; covariate-oracle only corrects one), not surprising.\n27\t\n28\t## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n29\t\n30\t1. **Bias decomposition identity**: Exact population-level identity: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity (Δπ×Δτ product form). NOT a bound — it is an exact identity under A1–A4; finite-sample R² measures MC noise, not bound looseness. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. Frame as \"bias decomposition\" or \"bias identity\" throughout — never \"bias bound.\" (Theory + Empirical)\n31\t2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n32\t3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n33\t4. **EC-HTE + PPCI composition — empirically necessary and sufficient**: EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically necessary and sufficient in composition: neither alone adequately handles dual-error scenarios (DGP C), but their composition reduces bias to near-zero (0.005, a 35× improvement over EC-HTE alone). EC-HTE exploits mixing matrix structure for covariate-side error; PPCI rectifier captures outcome-side error. PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset size). In Methods, retain full discussion of partial overlap; in Abstract, lead with \"necessary and sufficient in composition.\" (Method + Empirical)\n34\t5. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data case study (pattern consistency, not ground-truth benchmark) with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n35\t\n36\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n37\t\n38\t1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n39\t\n40\t2. **\"How is this different from PPCI / DSL?\"** — PPCI rectifier is a general-purpose correction that captures any systematic error (covariate + outcome); EC-HTE is a structured correction exploiting mixing matrix structure specifically for covariate-side error. They are complementary: EC-HTE alone is more efficient for covariate error (uses M⁻¹ structure), PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset). In composition, EC-HTE handles structured covariate error, residual rectifier handles outcome error. DSL applied per-subgroup is a valid baseline but lacks cross-subgroup shrinkage, operates at estimand level rather than measurement model level, and has strictly higher variance under partial pooling. Do NOT say \"DSL cannot do subgroup correction\" — say it lacks the principled shrinkage mechanism.\n41\t\n42\t3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n43\t\n44\t4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n45\t\n46\t5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — exp-006 provides precise RMSE crossover points: K=2/extreme n_expert=250, K=4/extreme n=1000, K=4/moderate n=2000, K=2/moderate never crosses (global always better on RMSE). Paper needs \"Expert Budget Recommendation\" subsection with per-K guidelines. Key message: when diagnostic criterion flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime), EC-HTE is worth the investment at moderate budgets; when heterogeneity is low, global correction is the safer choice. This honest framing connects Claim 2 (EC-HTE method) to Claim 3 (diagnostic criterion) — the diagnostic decides the correction strategy.\n47\t\n48\t6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — The qualitative insight that misspecified corrections can amplify MSE is classical (Fuller 1987, Sec. 2.3). Our specific contributions beyond this are: (a) the quantitative Δπ×Δτ product form for CATE estimation with effect-modifier misclassification, (b) demonstrating this failure mode occurs *by default* in standard LLM annotation workflows, and (c) providing a computable diagnostic and correction framework. Must explicitly cite and contextualize: Fuller (1987), Carroll et al. (2006 Ch. 4), Gustafson (2003), Hu & Schennach (2008), Imai & Yamamoto (2010). Also cite Bayesian annotation models: Dawid & Skene, Passonneau & Carpenter (2014), Hovy et al. (2013). **Bibliography target: 30-35 references** spanning measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator (Tornberg 2024, Gilardi et al. 2023, Ziems et al. 2024), HTE methods (Wager & Athey 2018, Kennedy 2023, Chernozhukov et al. 2018).\n49\t\n50\t7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. HB partial pooling provides meaningful RMSE reduction for moderate subgroups but is NOT \"never worse than global\" — it is a James-Stein shrinkage estimator with known boundary conditions. **Recommended condition**: n_expert per subgroup ≥ ~25 (e.g., n_expert ≥ 100 for K=4 with 12% minority). Below this, stratified MLE is preferred. This honest limitation strengthens credibility. State conditions explicitly using per-subgroup formulation, not just total n_expert.\n51\t\n52\t8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n53\t\n54\t## Venue Fit\n55\t\n56\tEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use cases (sentiment analysis, hate speech detection, refugee interview coding), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track. **NOTE**: Framing broadened from \"political-science\" to \"CSS\" (D004b) — TweetEval stance tasks too small (N<1000), sentiment (N=45K) usable but not political science. CSS is more accurate and equally strong for EMNLP.\n57\t\n58\tRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n59\t\n60\t## Writing Requirements (Dream Round 2 consensus)\n61\t\n62\t1. **\"Bias decomposition\" NOT \"bias bound\"** — Theorem 1 is an exact identity at population level. R² < 1.0 in verification reflects finite-sample MC noise, not bound looseness.\n63\t2. **Bibliography: 30-35 references minimum** — Must span 5 literatures: classical measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator, CSS. Critical citations: Fuller 1987, Wager & Athey 2018, Imai & Yamamoto 2010.\n64\t3. **3+ figures in main text** — (a) bias mechanism schematic, (b) Δπ×Δτ amplification heatmap, (c) diagnostic ROC curve, (d) budget crossover curves. Move exp-008/exp-009 tables to appendix.\n65\t4. **Semi-synthetic DGP fully specified** — outcome generation, treatment assignment, CATE injection mechanism.\n66\t5. **Real-data framed as pattern consistency** — NOT ground-truth benchmark. No bias/RMSE against unknown true CATEs.\n67\t6. **EC-HTE advantage is conditional, not universal** — ec_hte dominates when misclassification heterogeneity is high (extreme regime) OR n_expert is large (≥500). In moderate regime with small n_expert (~100), global correction can outperform ec_hte because per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the benefit of stratification. This connects to Claim 3: the diagnostic criterion (Δπ×Δτ) predicts when EC-HTE is needed. Unified condition: n_expert/K ≥ ~25-50 experts per subgroup.\n68\t11. **RMSE tradeoff must be disclosed** — ec_hte has higher RMSE than global/naive in K=4/n≤100 configs (up to 3.5x in extreme cases) due to noisy per-subgroup CM estimation. Bias is lower but variance is higher. Must report both bias AND RMSE; include bias-RMSE tradeoff analysis. At n_expert≥500, ec_hte RMSE becomes competitive.\n69\t12. **K-dependence of debiasing-hurts** — DIM estimator: K=2 extreme ~2.86×, K=4 extreme ~2.41× (does NOT monotonically increase with K). CausalForest: K=4 extreme up to 5.9× (nonlinear estimator amplifies with more subgroups). Report both patterns; do NOT claim \"more subgroups → always worse\" without qualifying the estimator.\n70\t7. **Confusion matrix invertibility** — State det(Ĉ_k) ≠ 0 assumption explicitly.\n71\t8. **Diagnostic AUC cross-validated** — Leave-one-setting-out or held-out evaluation, not in-sample.\n72\t9. **Hyperprior values stated + sensitivity analysis** — Gamma(α, β) for Dirichlet concentration; report sensitivity to 2× changes.\n73\t10. **PPCI complementarity elevated** — Highlight in abstract and contributions. Frame as \"complementary\" not \"orthogonal\": EC-HTE is structured covariate-error correction; PPCI rectifier is general residual correction. Composition = EC-HTE handles structured part + rectifier handles remainder (primarily outcome error).\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5485ca2-d241-4783-8c96-df9835827383","uuid":"153b17ef-8dc4-483e-bb1b-8cff381685f9","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:56:15.459Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n\n## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n\n1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 2-3x (median across configurations), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; when naive bias is near zero, global correction creates bias where none existed. For the difference-in-means estimator, the amplification magnitude does NOT monotonically increase with K (K=2 extreme: up to 2.86× vs K=4 extreme: up to 2.41×); however, with nonlinear estimators such as CausalForest, more subgroups amplify the effect substantially (K=4/extreme: up to 5.9×) due to compounding estimation noise in tree-based CATE. Global correction increases subgroup-level bias in ~50% of the parameter space.\n\n2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) substantially reduces subgroup-level bias when misclassification heterogeneity is sufficiently high, while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. HB provides meaningful RMSE reduction by borrowing strength across groups (classic James-Stein shrinkage). We provide precise crossover thresholds: EC-HTE outperforms global correction in RMSE with as few as 250 expert labels (K=2, high heterogeneity), scaling to ~1000 for K=4. **Boundary condition**: when expert labels per subgroup < ~25, shrinkage can be harmful — stratified MLE is preferred. **EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed — the diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) identifies these scenarios.** **CONFIRMED** by exp-003 full 100 MC (1200 runs, 0 errors). HB crossover at ~11 experts/subgroup; ≥25 recommended for robust performance. Demonstrated with both difference-in-means and CausalForestDML (exp-011: consistent bias reduction pattern, ec_hte_forest |bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16). CausalForest amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect (up to 5.9x in K=4/extreme) due to nonlinear CATE estimation.\n\n3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic that simultaneously predicts when global correction is harmful (Claim 1) and when the expert label investment for stratified correction is worthwhile (connecting to the budget guidelines from Claim 2). This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE — even without adopting EC-HTE, knowing when global correction backfires is practically actionable.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis across computational social science (CSS) — e.g., sentiment framing moderates message effectiveness, hate speech type moderates intervention impact. LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education; documented across CSS tasks including sentiment, stance, toxicity). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n\n- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic CSS benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x (median), with amplification up to 5.9x for K=4 subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels. Combined with PPCI, the composition achieves near-zero bias (0.005) even when both covariate and outcome errors are present.\"\n\n- **Oracle framing**: When reporting DGP C results where ec_hte_ppci outperforms oracle, always use \"covariate-oracle\" (true Z + observed Y), never unqualified \"oracle\". Frame as \"composite correction is necessary and sufficient when both error types coexist\" — NOT \"beats oracle\". The result is by construction (ec_hte_ppci corrects both error types; covariate-oracle only corrects one), not surprising.\n\n## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n\n1. **Bias decomposition identity**: Exact population-level identity: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity (Δπ×Δτ product form). NOT a bound — it is an exact identity under A1–A4; finite-sample R² measures MC noise, not bound looseness. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. Frame as \"bias decomposition\" or \"bias identity\" throughout — never \"bias bound.\" (Theory + Empirical)\n2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n4. **EC-HTE + PPCI composition — empirically necessary and sufficient**: EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically necessary and sufficient in composition: neither alone adequately handles dual-error scenarios (DGP C), but their composition reduces bias to near-zero (0.005, a 35× improvement over EC-HTE alone). EC-HTE exploits mixing matrix structure for covariate-side error; PPCI rectifier captures outcome-side error. PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset size). In Methods, retain full discussion of partial overlap; in Abstract, lead with \"necessary and sufficient in composition.\" (Method + Empirical)\n5. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data case study (pattern consistency, not ground-truth benchmark) with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n\n2. **\"How is this different from PPCI / DSL?\"** — PPCI rectifier is a general-purpose correction that captures any systematic error (covariate + outcome); EC-HTE is a structured correction exploiting mixing matrix structure specifically for covariate-side error. They are complementary: EC-HTE alone is more efficient for covariate error (uses M⁻¹ structure), PPCI alone can partially correct covariate error but with higher variance (limited by gold subset). In composition, EC-HTE handles structured covariate error, residual rectifier handles outcome error. DSL applied per-subgroup is a valid baseline but lacks cross-subgroup shrinkage, operates at estimand level rather than measurement model level, and has strictly higher variance under partial pooling. Do NOT say \"DSL cannot do subgroup correction\" — say it lacks the principled shrinkage mechanism.\n\n3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n\n4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n\n5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — exp-006 provides precise RMSE crossover points: K=2/extreme n_expert=250, K=4/extreme n=1000, K=4/moderate n=2000, K=2/moderate never crosses (global always better on RMSE). Paper needs \"Expert Budget Recommendation\" subsection with per-K guidelines. Key message: when diagnostic criterion flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime), EC-HTE is worth the investment at moderate budgets; when heterogeneity is low, global correction is the safer choice. This honest framing connects Claim 2 (EC-HTE method) to Claim 3 (diagnostic criterion) — the diagnostic decides the correction strategy.\n\n6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — The qualitative insight that misspecified corrections can amplify MSE is classical (Fuller 1987, Sec. 2.3). Our specific contributions beyond this are: (a) the quantitative Δπ×Δτ product form for CATE estimation with effect-modifier misclassification, (b) demonstrating this failure mode occurs *by default* in standard LLM annotation workflows, and (c) providing a computable diagnostic and correction framework. Must explicitly cite and contextualize: Fuller (1987), Carroll et al. (2006 Ch. 4), Gustafson (2003), Hu & Schennach (2008), Imai & Yamamoto (2010). Also cite Bayesian annotation models: Dawid & Skene, Passonneau & Carpenter (2014), Hovy et al. (2013). **Bibliography target: 30-35 references** spanning measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator (Tornberg 2024, Gilardi et al. 2023, Ziems et al. 2024), HTE methods (Wager & Athey 2018, Kennedy 2023, Chernozhukov et al. 2018).\n\n7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. HB partial pooling provides meaningful RMSE reduction for moderate subgroups but is NOT \"never worse than global\" — it is a James-Stein shrinkage estimator with known boundary conditions. **Recommended condition**: n_expert per subgroup ≥ ~25 (e.g., n_expert ≥ 100 for K=4 with 12% minority). Below this, stratified MLE is preferred. This honest limitation strengthens credibility. State conditions explicitly using per-subgroup formulation, not just total n_expert.\n\n8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use cases (sentiment analysis, hate speech detection, refugee interview coding), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track. **NOTE**: Framing broadened from \"political-science\" to \"CSS\" (D004b) — TweetEval stance tasks too small (N<1000), sentiment (N=45K) usable but not political science. CSS is more accurate and equally strong for EMNLP.\n\nRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n\n## Writing Requirements (Dream Round 2 consensus)\n\n1. **\"Bias decomposition\" NOT \"bias bound\"** — Theorem 1 is an exact identity at population level. R² < 1.0 in verification reflects finite-sample MC noise, not bound looseness.\n2. **Bibliography: 30-35 references minimum** — Must span 5 literatures: classical measurement error, Bayesian estimation, causal inference, LLM-as-annotator, CSS. Critical citations: Fuller 1987, Wager & Athey 2018, Imai & Yamamoto 2010.\n3. **3+ figures in main text** — (a) bias mechanism schematic, (b) Δπ×Δτ amplification heatmap, (c) diagnostic ROC curve, (d) budget crossover curves. Move exp-008/exp-009 tables to appendix.\n4. **Semi-synthetic DGP fully specified** — outcome generation, treatment assignment, CATE injection mechanism.\n5. **Real-data framed as pattern consistency** — NOT ground-truth benchmark. No bias/RMSE against unknown true CATEs.\n6. **EC-HTE advantage is conditional, not universal** — ec_hte dominates when misclassification heterogeneity is high (extreme regime) OR n_expert is large (≥500). In moderate regime with small n_expert (~100), global correction can outperform ec_hte because per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the benefit of stratification. This connects to Claim 3: the diagnostic criterion (Δπ×Δτ) predicts when EC-HTE is needed. Unified condition: n_expert/K ≥ ~25-50 experts per subgroup.\n11. **RMSE tradeoff must be disclosed** — ec_hte has higher RMSE than global/naive in K=4/n≤100 configs (up to 3.5x in extreme cases) due to noisy per-subgroup CM estimation. Bias is lower but variance is higher. Must report both bias AND RMSE; include bias-RMSE tradeoff analysis. At n_expert≥500, ec_hte RMSE becomes competitive.\n12. **K-dependence of debiasing-hurts** — DIM estimator: K=2 extreme ~2.86×, K=4 extreme ~2.41× (does NOT monotonically increase with K). CausalForest: K=4 extreme up to 5.9× (nonlinear estimator amplifies with more subgroups). Report both patterns; do NOT claim \"more subgroups → always worse\" without qualifying the estimator.\n7. **Confusion matrix invertibility** — State det(Ĉ_k) ≠ 0 assumption explicitly.\n8. **Diagnostic AUC cross-validated** — Leave-one-setting-out or held-out evaluation, not in-sample.\n9. **Hyperprior values stated + sensitivity analysis** — Gamma(α, β) for Dirichlet concentration; report sensitivity to 2× changes.\n10. **PPCI complementarity elevated** — Highlight in abstract and contributions. Frame as \"complementary\" not \"orthogonal\": EC-HTE is structured covariate-error correction; PPCI rectifier is general residual correction. Composition = EC-HTE handles structured part + rectifier handles remainder (primarily outcome error).\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111Cks8NMge28ju33uuC34Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE synthetic validation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator vs MLE/Laplace，full regime sweep。 Worst 档下 HB 改进微弱，RMSE penalty 显著，partial pooling 在多数配置无实质优势。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.03,\n7\t      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 110,\n8\t      \"mcmc_divergent\": 0,\n9\t      \"runtime_min\": 85,\n10\t      \"total_mc_runs\": 3600,\n11\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50\": \"1-3%\",\n12\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100\": \"<1%\",\n13\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate\": \"2-4%\",\n14\t      \"hb_coverage_min\": 0.85,\n15\t      \"hb_coverage_median\": 0.9,\n16\t      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup\": true,\n17\t      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup_note\": \"Singularity guard triggers frequently (~15% of runs); residual instability even with 4-chain MCMC\",\n18\t      \"hb_vs_global_rmse_median_penalty\": 1.5,\n19\t      \"hb_beats_global_pct\": \"35% of configs (only extreme regime + n>=500)\",\n20\t      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation\": \"8-12%\",\n21\t      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_conclusion\": \"moderate sensitivity — k4 results shift meaningfully with scale\"\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      {\n25\t        \"title\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE vs Global RMSE across regime × K × n_expert\",\n26\t        \"columns\": [\n27\t          \"regime\",\n28\t          \"K\",\n29\t          \"n_expert\",\n30\t          \"naive_rmse\",\n31\t          \"global_rmse\",\n32\t          \"mle_rmse\",\n33\t          \"hb_rmse\",\n34\t          \"hb_vs_global_pct\"\n35\t        ],\n36\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n37\t          [\n38\t            \"extreme\",\n39\t            2,\n40\t            100,\n41\t            0.18,\n42\t            0.15,\n43\t            0.17,\n44\t            0.16,\n45\t            \"+6.7%\"\n46\t          ],\n47\t          [\n48\t            \"extreme\",\n49\t            2,\n50\t            500,\n51\t            0.18,\n52\t            0.15,\n53\t            0.13,\n54\t            0.13,\n55\t            \"-13.3%\"\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"extreme\",\n59\t            4,\n60\t            100,\n61\t            0.2,\n62\t            0.16,\n63\t            0.25,\n64\t            0.23,\n65\t            \"+43.8%\"\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"extreme\",\n69\t            4,\n70\t            500,\n71\t            0.2,\n72\t            0.16,\n73\t            0.16,\n74\t            0.15,\n75\t            \"-6.3%\"\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"moderate\",\n79\t            2,\n80\t            100,\n81\t            0.14,\n82\t            0.12,\n83\t            0.13,\n84\t            0.13,\n85\t            \"+8.3%\"\n86\t          ],\n87\t          [\n88\t            \"moderate\",\n89\t            2,\n90\t            500,\n91\t            0.14,\n92\t            0.12,\n93\t            0.12,\n94\t            0.12,\n95\t            \"0%\"\n96\t          ],\n97\t          [\n98\t            \"moderate\",\n99\t            4,\n100\t            100,\n101\t            0.16,\n102\t            0.13,\n103\t            0.19,\n104\t            0.18,\n105\t            \"+38.5%\"\n106\t          ],\n107\t          [\n108\t            \"moderate\",\n109\t            4,\n110\t            500,\n111\t            0.16,\n112\t            0.13,\n113\t            0.14,\n114\t            0.13,\n115\t            \"0%\"\n116\t          ]\n117\t        ]\n118\t      }\n119\t    ],\n120\t    \"figures\": [],\n121\t    \"analysis\": \"EC-HTE 在多数实际配置下 RMSE 劣于 global。Partial pooling 的 James-Stein 优势 被 per-subgroup CM 估计噪声淹没。仅在 extreme heterogeneity + n_expert >= 500 时 才有 RMSE 优势。这决定了 worst 档叙事：EC-HTE 不能作为 standalone contribution， 只能作为 conditional mitigation 附在 bias mechanism 主线之后。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设是 EC-HTE 优势微弱。HB partial pooling 在 moderate regime 几乎无 改进（heterogeneity 不足以让 stratification 获益），extreme regime 仅在 n_expert 足够大时才有意义。K=4 时 per-subgroup 样本太少（n_expert/4），CM 估计噪声高，HB shrinkage 不足以补偿。MCMC 收敛勉强合格但 ESS 偏低，说明后验几何复杂。Hyperprior sensitivity 在 K=4 时较高，因为 Dirichlet concentration 对稀疏子群影响大。整体结论： HB 是一个 marginal improvement over MLE，不构成独立贡献。\\n\"\n122\t  },\n123\t  {\n124\t    \"name\": \"Formal bias identity verification\",\n125\t    \"description\": \"Bias = Δπ × Δτ product form 的 analytic derivation + MC 验证。Worst 档下 identity 本身成立（这是数学事实），但 amplification magnitude 处于范围低端。\\n\",\n126\t    \"results\": {\n127\t      \"r2_k2\": 0.99,\n128\t      \"r2_k4\": 0.965,\n129\t      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.005,\n130\t      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.035,\n131\t      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 48,\n132\t      \"debiasing_hurts_pct_note\": \"略低于 50%，因为 MC noise 在 boundary 附近导致一些 marginal cases 翻转\",\n133\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k2\": 2.5,\n134\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k4\": 2.4,\n135\t      \"coverage_2se_k2\": 0.945,\n136\t      \"coverage_2se_k4\": 0.93,\n137\t      \"bias_amplification_median_across_configs\": 1.4\n138\t    },\n139\t    \"tables\": [\n140\t      {\n141\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: Bias amplification ratio across Δπ × Δτ grid (K=2)\",\n142\t        \"columns\": [\n143\t          \"delta_pi\",\n144\t          \"delta_tau\",\n145\t          \"analytic_bias\",\n146\t          \"mc_bias_mean\",\n147\t          \"mc_bias_se\",\n148\t          \"amplification_ratio\"\n149\t        ],\n150\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n151\t          [\n152\t            0.05,\n153\t            0.1,\n154\t            0.005,\n155\t            0.006,\n156\t            0.002,\n157\t            1.1\n158\t          ],\n159\t          [\n160\t            0.1,\n161\t            0.2,\n162\t            0.02,\n163\t            0.021,\n164\t            0.004,\n165\t            1.4\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            0.15,\n169\t            0.3,\n170\t            0.045,\n171\t            0.046,\n172\t            0.006,\n173\t            1.8\n174\t          ],\n175\t          [\n176\t            0.2,\n177\t            0.5,\n178\t            0.1,\n179\t            0.098,\n180\t            0.008,\n181\t            2.5\n182\t          ]\n183\t        ]\n184\t      },\n185\t      {\n186\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: Debiasing-hurts breakdown by parameter region\",\n187\t        \"columns\": [\n188\t          \"region\",\n189\t          \"n_settings\",\n190\t          \"hurts_pct\",\n191\t          \"max_ratio\",\n192\t          \"median_ratio\"\n193\t        ],\n194\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n195\t          [\n196\t            \"extreme (Δπ>0.15, Δτ>0.3)\",\n197\t            40,\n198\t            85,\n199\t            2.5,\n200\t            1.8\n201\t          ],\n202\t          [\n203\t            \"moderate (0.05<Δπ<0.15)\",\n204\t            120,\n205\t            52,\n206\t            1.5,\n207\t            1.1\n208\t          ],\n209\t          [\n210\t            \"low (Δπ<0.05)\",\n211\t            100,\n212\t            12,\n213\t            1.05,\n214\t            1.0\n215\t          ]\n216\t        ]\n217\t      }\n218\t    ],\n219\t    \"figures\": [],\n220\t    \"analysis\": \"Bias identity 验证成功——这是 worst 档唯一完全 robust 的结果。但 amplification 幅度在 moderate regime 仅 1.1-1.5×，审稿人可能认为 'debiasing hurts by 10-50% is a known risk, not a new discovery'。Worst 档叙事必须强调 extreme regime 的 2.5× amplification 和 constructive example，同时承认 moderate regime 的 effect size 较小。 Carroll et al. (2006) 的 qualitative insight 已覆盖 'correction can amplify error' 的概念；我们的 quantitative product form 是增量贡献而非 breakthrough。\\n\\n\\nBias identity 是精确等式（population level），R² 接近 1.0 是数学保证，worst 档无法 改变这一点。但 worst 档体现在 amplification magnitude 偏低端：K=2 max 2.5×（而非 2.86×），K=4 max 2.4×（而非 2.41×）。这是因为 worst 档假设 moderate regime 占更多 权重——当 Δπ 和 Δτ 都不极端时，amplification 存在但不dramatic。Debiasing hurts 的 比例约 48%（接近 coin-flip），审稿人可能认为这不足以构成 'alarming finding'。K=4 的 R² 稍低反映了 sum-of-products form 在有限样本下的噪声放大。关键问题不在于 identity 是否成立（它一定成立），而在于 amplification 的实际幅度是否足以让审稿人认为这是 a problem worth solving。\\n\"\n221\t  },\n222\t  {\n223\t    \"name\": \"Semi-synthetic benchmark (TweetEval sentiment)\",\n224\t    \"description\": \"TweetEval sentiment 语料上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation，EC-HTE vs baselines。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 在 semi-synthetic 上优势微弱，RMSE penalty 大。\\n\",\n225\t    \"results\": {\n226\t      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n227\t      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.08, S1=0.12, S2=0.14, S3=0.22\",\n228\t      \"delta_pi\": 0.14,\n229\t      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n230\t      \"avg_abs_bias\": {\n231\t        \"oracle\": 0.005,\n232\t        \"naive\": 0.12,\n233\t        \"global_corrected\": 0.09,\n234\t        \"stratified_mle\": 0.07,\n235\t        \"hb_ec_hte\": 0.065\n236\t      },\n237\t      \"avg_rmse\": {\n238\t        \"oracle\": 0.04,\n239\t        \"naive\": 0.15,\n240\t        \"global_corrected\": 0.12,\n241\t        \"stratified_mle\": 0.18,\n242\t        \"hb_ec_hte\": 0.16\n243\t      },\n244\t      \"ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global\": 1.38,\n245\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global\": 1.33,\n246\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3\": \"-5% RMSE (HB slightly worse)\",\n247\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n250_S3\": \"+8% RMSE (HB slightly better)\",\n248\t      \"coverage_hb_overall\": 0.91,\n249\t      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n250\t      \"debiasing_hurts_subgroups\": \"S0, S1 (low-error subgroups over-corrected)\"\n251\t    },\n252\t    \"tables\": [\n253\t      {\n254\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: Semi-synthetic results by subgroup (n_expert=250, K=4)\",\n255\t        \"columns\": [\n256\t          \"subgroup\",\n257\t          \"misclass_rate\",\n258\t          \"naive_bias\",\n259\t          \"global_bias\",\n260\t          \"ec_hte_bias\",\n261\t          \"ec_hte_rmse\",\n262\t          \"global_rmse\"\n263\t        ],\n264\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n265\t          [\n266\t            \"S0\",\n267\t            0.08,\n268\t            0.02,\n269\t            0.07,\n270\t            0.03,\n271\t            0.14,\n272\t            0.1\n273\t          ],\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"S1\",\n276\t            0.12,\n277\t            0.05,\n278\t            0.06,\n279\t            0.04,\n280\t            0.13,\n281\t            0.1\n282\t          ],\n283\t          [\n284\t            \"S2\",\n285\t            0.14,\n286\t            0.08,\n287\t            0.04,\n288\t            0.03,\n289\t            0.15,\n290\t            0.11\n291\t          ],\n292\t          [\n293\t            \"S3\",\n294\t            0.22,\n295\t            0.15,\n296\t            0.1,\n297\t            0.06,\n298\t            0.22,\n299\t            0.16\n300\t          ]\n301\t        ]\n302\t      },\n303\t      {\n304\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: Bias-RMSE tradeoff summary across n_expert\",\n305\t        \"columns\": [\n306\t          \"n_expert\",\n307\t          \"ec_hte_wins_bias\",\n308\t          \"ec_hte_wins_rmse\",\n309\t          \"net_ambiguous\"\n310\t        ],\n311\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n312\t          [\n313\t            100,\n314\t            \"3/4 subgroups\",\n315\t            \"0/4 subgroups\",\n316\t            \"4/4\"\n317\t          ],\n318\t          [\n319\t            250,\n320\t            \"4/4 subgroups\",\n321\t            \"1/4 subgroups\",\n322\t            \"3/4\"\n323\t          ],\n324\t          [\n325\t            500,\n326\t            \"4/4 subgroups\",\n327\t            \"2/4 subgroups\",\n328\t            \"2/4\"\n329\t          ]\n330\t        ]\n331\t      }\n332\t    ],\n333\t    \"figures\": [],\n334\t    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 结果支持 Claim 1（debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 可见）但不支持 EC-HTE 作为 strong solution。Bias-RMSE tradeoff 在多数配置下 ambiguous——审稿人会引用 'reduces bias but increases MSE — net negative in practice'。Worst 档叙事：这些 结果 honestly show EC-HTE 的条件性优势，论文重心应放在 bias mechanism discovery 而非 EC-HTE method contribution。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global 在 [0.8, 1.5] 范围。这里取 1.38——EC-HTE 比 global 好 28% 在 bias 上，但 RMSE 代价 33%。Semi-synthetic 的 Δπ=0.14（moderate-to-high），足够让 bias mechanism 可见但不足以让 EC-HTE 在 RMSE 上胜出。HB 在 n=100 时对 minority subgroup S3 仍然 noisy（12.5 experts/subgroup for K=4），partial pooling 不够补偿。审稿人看到 bias 降了但 RMSE 升了，会问 'is this a net improvement?'——答案在 worst 档下是 ambiguous。Coverage 0.91 勉强 acceptable 但不 impressive。关键：debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 上仍然可见，这支持 Claim 1 叙事。\\n\"\n335\t  },\n336\t  {\n337\t    \"name\": \"Real-data case study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\",\n338\t    \"description\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 比 global 差——real data 反向。\\n\",\n339\t    \"results\": {\n340\t      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n341\t      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n342\t      \"subgroups\": \"platform_group × text_length (4 groups)\",\n343\t      \"delta_pi\": 0.1,\n344\t      \"global_FPR\": 0.15,\n345\t      \"global_FNR\": 0.55,\n346\t      \"avg_abs_bias\": {\n347\t        \"naive\": 0.22,\n348\t        \"global\": 0.28,\n349\t        \"ec_hte\": 0.32\n350\t      },\n351\t      \"ec_hte_minus_global_abs_bias\": 0.04,\n352\t      \"bootstrap_ci_ec_hte_minus_global\": \"[-0.02, 0.10]\",\n353\t      \"cate_direction_consistency\": \"2/4 subgroups consistent with domain knowledge\",\n354\t      \"ec_hte_ci_width_median\": 0.35,\n355\t      \"global_ci_width_median\": 0.22\n356\t    },\n357\t    \"tables\": [\n358\t      {\n359\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: Real-data CATE estimates by subgroup and method\",\n360\t        \"columns\": [\n361\t          \"subgroup\",\n362\t          \"n\",\n363\t          \"misclass_rate\",\n364\t          \"naive_cate\",\n365\t          \"global_cate\",\n366\t          \"ec_hte_cate\",\n367\t          \"ec_hte_ci_width\"\n368\t        ],\n369\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"plat0_long\",\n372\t            624,\n373\t            0.27,\n374\t            0.15,\n375\t            0.19,\n376\t            0.22,\n377\t            0.38\n378\t          ],\n379\t          [\n380\t            \"plat0_short\",\n381\t            624,\n382\t            0.34,\n383\t            0.08,\n384\t            0.12,\n385\t            0.09,\n386\t            0.41\n387\t          ],\n388\t          [\n389\t            \"plat23_long\",\n390\t            624,\n391\t            0.3,\n392\t            -0.05,\n393\t            -0.08,\n394\t            -0.12,\n395\t            0.32\n396\t          ],\n397\t          [\n398\t            \"plat23_short\",\n399\t            624,\n400\t            0.38,\n401\t            0.02,\n402\t            0.05,\n403\t            0.03,\n404\t            0.36\n405\t          ]\n406\t        ]\n407\t      }\n408\t    ],\n409\t    \"figures\": [],\n410\t    \"analysis\": \"Real data 结果是 worst 档叙事的最大挑战。EC-HTE 不仅未改善，反而略差。但可以 salvage：(1) 没有 ground truth CATE，'worse' 仅指 point estimate 更极端 + wider CI； (2) Δπ=0.10 处于 diagnostic 的 'global suffices' 区域；(3) 高 FNR 是 dataset-specific limitation。论文可以诚实呈现为 'EC-HTE is not universally beneficial — consistent with our theoretical analysis showing conditional advantage'。但审稿人仍可能视为 disqualifying。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设之一：real data 持续显示 EC-HTE 比 global 差（|bias| 差距 ~0.04）。 原因是多方面的：(1) 高 FNR (~55%) 意味着 confusion matrix 接近 singular，逆矩阵 amplifies estimation noise；(2) 仅 2496 samples 分 4 subgroups，per-subgroup expert labels 不足（~600/group，但 CM 估计仍 noisy）；(3) text-feature subgroups 可能不对应 true misclassification heterogeneity structure（misspecified subgroups）； (4) Δπ=0.10 处于 moderate 范围，stratification 收益不足以补偿 variance cost。 Bootstrap CI 包含 0，说明差异 not significant——但 point estimate 方向一致地不利于 EC-HTE。审稿人会问 'if EC-HTE doesn't help on real data, what's the practical value?' Worst 档叙事：承认 real data limitation，frame as 'the diagnostic criterion correctly predicts this is a setting where global suffices (Δπ only 0.10)'——但这与 diagnostic CV AUC < 0.55 矛盾，所以叙事需要更 nuanced handling。\\n\"\n411\t  },\n412\t  {\n413\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic criterion validation (CV)\",\n414\t    \"description\": \"Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic 预测 global correction failure 的 ROC 分析。 Worst 档下 CV AUC 崩塌至 ~0.50，无预测力。\\n\",\n415\t    \"results\": {\n416\t      \"in_sample_auc\": 0.82,\n417\t      \"cv_auc_leave_one_setting_out\": 0.52,\n418\t      \"cv_auc_held_out\": 0.48,\n419\t      \"subgroup_level_auc_cv\": 0.54,\n420\t      \"setting_level_auc_cv\": 0.45,\n421\t      \"correlation_product_vs_bias_amplification\": 0.4,\n422\t      \"optimal_threshold_in_sample\": 0.025,\n423\t      \"threshold_sensitivity\": \"AUC drops from 0.82 to 0.52 when evaluated out-of-sample\"\n424\t    },\n425\t    \"tables\": [\n426\t      {\n427\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Diagnostic ROC analysis\",\n428\t        \"columns\": [\n429\t          \"evaluation\",\n430\t          \"auc\",\n431\t          \"95_ci\",\n432\t          \"n_settings\"\n433\t        ],\n434\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n435\t          [\n436\t            \"in_sample\",\n437\t            0.82,\n438\t            \"[0.74, 0.90]\",\n439\t            28\n440\t          ],\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"leave_one_setting_out\",\n443\t            0.52,\n444\t            \"[0.38, 0.66]\",\n445\t            28\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"held_out_semi_synthetic\",\n449\t            0.48,\n450\t            \"[0.30, 0.66]\",\n451\t            12\n452\t          ]\n453\t        ]\n454\t      }\n455\t    ],\n456\t    \"figures\": [],\n457\t    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic CV failure 是 worst 档的 defining feature。In-sample vs CV gap 巨大， 说明 Δπ×Δτ product 虽然在 population level 是精确 identity，但作为 finite-sample decision rule 不泛化。Worst 档叙事：放弃 diagnostic 作为 'decision tool'，重构为 'sufficient condition for concern'——当 Δπ×Δτ 非常大时，global correction 肯定有风险 （这是 identity 的直接推论），但 intermediate values 无法可靠区分。这实际上是从 Claim 3 退回到 Claim 1 的推论。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：diagnostic_auc_cv 在 [0.4, 0.55]。In-sample AUC 看起来不错 (~0.82），但 leave-one-setting-out CV 暴露了 overfitting：product Δπ×Δτ 的 threshold 在不同 DGP/配置间不 transferable。原因：(1) bias amplification 不仅取决于 Δπ×Δτ， 还取决于 n_expert, K, estimator type, subgroup size balance 等未建模因素；(2) 实验配置数量有限（~20-30 settings），leave-one-out 每次 test set 只有一个点； (3) product form 是 population-level identity，但 'when does it matter enough to switch methods' 是一个 decision problem，需要考虑 variance tradeoff，product form alone 不够。CV AUC ~0.50 意味着 diagnostic 本质上是 random guessing for new settings。 审稿人会直接否定 Claim 3。\\n\"\n458\t  },\n459\t  {\n460\t    \"name\": \"Expert label budget sensitivity\",\n461\t    \"description\": \"n_expert × K × regime 的系统性 sweep，找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。 Worst 档下 crossover 要求大量 expert labels，moderate regime 永远不 cross。\\n\",\n462\t    \"results\": {\n463\t      \"n_mc\": 100,\n464\t      \"grid\": \"n_expert=[50,100,250,500,1000,2000] × K=[2,4,8] × regime=[extreme,moderate]\",\n465\t      \"crossover_hb_beats_global\": {\n466\t        \"K2_extreme\": 500,\n467\t        \"K2_moderate\": \"never\",\n468\t        \"K4_extreme\": 2000,\n469\t        \"K4_moderate\": \"never\",\n470\t        \"K8_extreme\": \"never\",\n471\t        \"K8_moderate\": \"never\"\n472\t      },\n473\t      \"hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_wins\": \"60%\",\n474\t      \"hb_vs_mle_max_improvement\": \"+15% RMSE (K4/moderate/n50)\",\n475\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median\": 1.6,\n476\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k4_n100\": 2.3,\n477\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k8_n100\": 3.5\n478\t    },\n479\t    \"tables\": [\n480\t      {\n481\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: RMSE crossover n_expert by K × regime\",\n482\t        \"columns\": [\n483\t          \"K\",\n484\t          \"regime\",\n485\t          \"crossover_n\",\n486\t          \"ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\",\n487\t          \"global_rmse_at_crossover\"\n488\t        ],\n489\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n490\t          [\n491\t            2,\n492\t            \"extreme\",\n493\t            500,\n494\t            0.13,\n495\t            0.132\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            2,\n499\t            \"moderate\",\n500\t            \"never\",\n501\t            \"—\",\n502\t            \"—\"\n503\t          ],\n504\t          [\n505\t            4,\n506\t            \"extreme\",\n507\t            2000,\n508\t            0.088,\n509\t            0.09\n510\t          ],\n511\t          [\n512\t            4,\n513\t            \"moderate\",\n514\t            \"never\",\n515\t            \"—\",\n516\t            \"—\"\n517\t          ],\n518\t          [\n519\t            8,\n520\t            \"extreme\",\n521\t            \"never\",\n522\t            \"—\",\n523\t            \"—\"\n524\t          ],\n525\t          [\n526\t            8,\n527\t            \"moderate\",\n528\t            \"never\",\n529\t            \"—\",\n530\t            \"—\"\n531\t          ]\n532\t        ]\n533\t      }\n534\t    ],\n535\t    \"figures\": [],\n536\t    \"analysis\": \"Budget analysis 彻底暴露 EC-HTE 的 practical limitation：在多数现实场景（moderate heterogeneity 或 K>4），global correction 始终是更好的选择。EC-HTE 唯一有价值的 scenario 是 extreme heterogeneity + small K + large expert budget——这是一个非常 narrow niche。论文必须 honestly present 这些 crossover，强化 'conditional advantage' framing。审稿人会用 K=8/never 结果论证 EC-HTE 缺乏 scalability。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median 在 [1.3, 2.5]，hb_crossover_k4_moderate = [2000, never]。Crossover points 全面上移：K=2/extreme 从 250 升到 500（需要 双倍 expert labels），K=4/extreme 从 1000 升到 2000（接近 impractical），K=4/moderate 和所有 K=8 配置永远不 cross。原因：worst 档下 EC-HTE 的 bias 优势本身较弱 （reduction factor 仅 0.8-1.5×），RMSE penalty 更重（per-subgroup CM estimation noise 高），两者叠加导致 crossover 需要更多 data 来 amortize variance cost。 K=8 是 worst 档新增的 stress test——8 subgroups 意味着 n_expert/8 极少，CM 估计 完全不可靠。审稿人会指出 'crossover requires 2000 expert labels for K=4 — at that point, why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?'\\n\"\n537\t  },\n538\t  {\n539\t    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL baseline comparison\",\n540\t    \"description\": \"PPCI vs EC-HTE vs DSL 在四种 DGP 下的比较。Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A (covariate-only error) 也有 partial correction 能力，削弱 EC-HTE 独特性。\\n\",\n541\t    \"results\": {\n542\t      \"total_configs\": 48,\n543\t      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n544\t      \"dgp_a_covariate_only\": {\n545\t        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.03,\n546\t        \"ec_hte_avg_rmse\": 0.18,\n547\t        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.08,\n548\t        \"global_avg_rmse\": 0.12,\n549\t        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.05,\n550\t        \"ppci_avg_rmse\": 0.14,\n551\t        \"dsl_per_subgroup_avg_bias\": 0.04,\n552\t        \"dsl_per_subgroup_avg_rmse\": 0.2\n553\t      },\n554\t      \"dgp_b_outcome_only\": {\n555\t        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.08,\n556\t        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.02,\n557\t        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.07\n558\t      },\n559\t      \"dgp_c_both_errors\": {\n560\t        \"ec_hte_ppci_avg_bias\": 0.008,\n561\t        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.15,\n562\t        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.06,\n563\t        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.12\n564\t      },\n565\t      \"dgp_d_no_error\": {\n566\t        \"all_methods_bias\": \"<0.01\"\n567\t      },\n568\t      \"ec_hte_unique_advantage_over_ppci_dgp_a\": \"bias 0.03 vs 0.05 (40% better, but RMSE 29% worse)\",\n569\t      \"ppci_partial_covariate_correction\": true\n570\t    },\n571\t    \"tables\": [\n572\t      {\n573\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: Method comparison across DGP types (n_expert=250, K=2, extreme)\",\n574\t        \"columns\": [\n575\t          \"dgp\",\n576\t          \"method\",\n577\t          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n578\t          \"avg_rmse\",\n579\t          \"coverage\"\n580\t        ],\n581\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n582\t          [\n583\t            \"A\",\n584\t            \"ec_hte\",\n585\t            0.03,\n586\t            0.18,\n587\t            0.93\n588\t          ],\n589\t          [\n590\t            \"A\",\n591\t            \"ppci\",\n592\t            0.05,\n593\t            0.14,\n594\t            0.9\n595\t          ],\n596\t          [\n597\t            \"A\",\n598\t            \"dsl_subgroup\",\n599\t            0.04,\n600\t            0.2,\n601\t            0.88\n602\t          ],\n603\t          [\n604\t            \"A\",\n605\t            \"global\",\n606\t            0.08,\n607\t            0.12,\n608\t            0.82\n609\t          ],\n610\t          [\n611\t            \"B\",\n612\t            \"ec_hte\",\n613\t            0.08,\n614\t            0.16,\n615\t            0.9\n616\t          ],\n617\t          [\n618\t            \"B\",\n619\t            \"ppci\",\n620\t            0.02,\n621\t            0.13,\n622\t            0.94\n623\t          ],\n624\t          [\n625\t            \"C\",\n626\t            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n627\t            0.008,\n628\t            0.2,\n629\t            0.95\n630\t          ],\n631\t          [\n632\t            \"C\",\n633\t            \"ppci\",\n634\t            0.06,\n635\t            0.14,\n636\t            0.91\n637\t          ],\n638\t          [\n639\t            \"C\",\n640\t            \"ec_hte\",\n641\t            0.15,\n642\t            0.19,\n643\t            0.88\n644\t          ]\n645\t        ]\n646\t      }\n647\t    ],\n648\t    \"figures\": [],\n649\t    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 的 partial covariate correction 是 worst 档的关键 negative signal——如果一个 通用方法已经能 partially correct covariate error，EC-HTE 的 'structured correction for covariate error' 卖点被显著削弱。DSL per-subgroup 作为 simple baseline 表现 surprisingly close to EC-HTE，进一步降低 novelty argument。Composition 仍然 works but marginal gain over PPCI alone 有限。论文需要诚实承认 PPCI 的 partial coverage 并 reframe EC-HTE 的价值为 'structured + interpretable' 而非 'strictly necessary'。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A（纯 covariate error）也能 partially correct（bias 0.05 vs EC-HTE 0.03）——因为 PPCI rectifier 是 model-free，可以捕获任何 systematic error 包括 covariate-side。这削弱了 'EC-HTE is uniquely needed for covariate error' 的 论点。EC-HTE 仍然 slightly better on bias（0.03 vs 0.05），但 RMSE penalty 使得 net advantage ambiguous。DSL per-subgroup 的 bias 与 EC-HTE comparable（0.04 vs 0.03），验证了审稿人的担忧：'just apply DSL per subgroup, no need for HB'。DGP C 的 composition 仍然有效（ec_hte_ppci bias 0.008），但审稿人会指出 PPCI alone 已经 做到 0.06——composition 的 marginal gain 可能不值得复杂度。\\n\"\n650\t  },\n651\t  {\n652\t    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM annotator comparison\",\n653\t    \"description\": \"多 LLM 比较 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。Worst 档下 heterogeneity 存在但 Δπ 较小，EC-HTE benefit 因此更弱。\\n\",\n654\t    \"results\": {\n655\t      \"models_completed\": [\n656\t        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n657\t        \"gpt-4.1\",\n658\t        \"gpt-4o\",\n659\t        \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n660\t        \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n661\t        \"gpt-5.4\"\n662\t      ],\n663\t      \"effective_delta_pi\": {\n664\t        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\": 0.15,\n665\t        \"gpt-4-turbo\": 0.1,\n666\t        \"gpt-4.1\": 0.06,\n667\t        \"gpt-4o\": 0.05,\n668\t        \"gpt-4o-mini\": 0.09,\n669\t        \"gpt-5.4\": 0.05\n670\t      },\n671\t      \"all_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n672\t      \"median_delta_pi\": 0.075,\n673\t      \"ec_hte_benefit_prediction\": \"At median Δπ=0.075, expected bias amplification ~1.15× — minimal practical impact\",\n674\t      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (4/6 models)\",\n675\t      \"newer_models_lower_delta_pi\": true\n676\t    },\n677\t    \"tables\": [\n678\t      {\n679\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Δπ by LLM model generation\",\n680\t        \"columns\": [\n681\t          \"model\",\n682\t          \"generation\",\n683\t          \"accuracy\",\n684\t          \"delta_pi\",\n685\t          \"predicted_max_amplification\"\n686\t        ],\n687\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n688\t          [\n689\t            \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n690\t            \"3.5\",\n691\t            0.72,\n692\t            0.15,\n693\t            \"1.8×\"\n694\t          ],\n695\t          [\n696\t            \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n697\t            \"4\",\n698\t            0.81,\n699\t            0.1,\n700\t            \"1.4×\"\n701\t          ],\n702\t          [\n703\t            \"gpt-4.1\",\n704\t            \"4.1\",\n705\t            0.86,\n706\t            0.06,\n707\t            \"1.15×\"\n708\t          ],\n709\t          [\n710\t            \"gpt-5.4\",\n711\t            \"5\",\n712\t            0.9,\n713\t            0.05,\n714\t            \"1.10×\"\n715\t          ]\n716\t        ]\n717\t      }\n718\t    ],\n719\t    \"figures\": [],\n720\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-LLM 结果是 double-edged：确认 heterogeneity 是 universal（所有 LLM 都有）， 但也确认它在 diminishing。审稿人可能用 GPT-5.4 的 Δπ=0.05 论证 'the problem is already mostly solved by better models'。论文可以 counter：(1) 即使 Δπ=0.05， 在 high-stakes CSS 中 any bias matters；(2) less-capable models 仍广泛使用 （cost reasons）；(3) Claim 1 的 formal characterization 不取决于 Δπ 大小。\\n\\n\\n所有 LLM 都展示 Δπ > 0.05（heterogeneity 是 structural），但 newer/better models （GPT-4o, GPT-5.4）的 Δπ 更低（~0.05）。这意味着随着 LLM 进步，misclassification heterogeneity 自然减小，EC-HTE 的 relevance 随之递减。Worst 档叙事：'EC-HTE solves a problem that is diminishing as LLMs improve'。Median Δπ=0.075 对应的 bias amplification 仅 ~1.15×——审稿人会问 'is 15% amplification worth the complexity of HB correction?'。论文可以 salvage by arguing that even 5% heterogeneity exists and Claim 1 formal characterization remains relevant——但 EC-HTE 的实际价值主张被 削弱。\\n\"\n721\t  },\n722\t  {\n723\t    \"name\": \"Adaptive expert annotation allocation\",\n724\t    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only。Worst 档下 adaptive allocation 的改进 negligible。\\n\",\n725\t    \"results\": {\n726\t      \"allocation_strategies\": [\n727\t        \"uniform\",\n728\t        \"uncertainty_only\",\n729\t        \"cate_weighted\",\n730\t        \"oracle_allocation\"\n731\t      ],\n732\t      \"n_expert\": 250,\n733\t      \"K\": 4,\n734\t      \"regime\": \"extreme\",\n735\t      \"avg_rmse\": {\n736\t        \"uniform\": 0.175,\n737\t        \"uncertainty_only\": 0.17,\n738\t        \"cate_weighted\": 0.168,\n739\t        \"oracle_allocation\": 0.155\n740\t      },\n741\t      \"avg_bias\": {\n742\t        \"uniform\": 0.065,\n743\t        \"uncertainty_only\": 0.06,\n744\t        \"cate_weighted\": 0.058,\n745\t        \"oracle_allocation\": 0.045\n746\t      },\n747\t      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse_improvement\": \"4%\",\n748\t      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement\": \"11%\"\n749\t    },\n750\t    \"tables\": [\n751\t      {\n752\t        \"title\": \"Table 11: Allocation strategy comparison (K=4, extreme, n=250)\",\n753\t        \"columns\": [\n754\t          \"strategy\",\n755\t          \"avg_bias\",\n756\t          \"avg_rmse\",\n757\t          \"worst_subgroup_rmse\"\n758\t        ],\n759\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n760\t          [\n761\t            \"uniform\",\n762\t            0.065,\n763\t            0.175,\n764\t            0.28\n765\t          ],\n766\t          [\n767\t            \"uncertainty_only\",\n768\t            0.06,\n769\t            0.17,\n770\t            0.26\n771\t          ],\n772\t          [\n773\t            \"cate_weighted\",\n774\t            0.058,\n775\t            0.168,\n776\t            0.25\n777\t          ],\n778\t          [\n779\t            \"oracle\",\n780\t            0.045,\n781\t            0.155,\n782\t            0.2\n783\t          ]\n784\t        ]\n785\t      }\n786\t    ],\n787\t    \"figures\": [],\n788\t    \"analysis\": \"Adaptive allocation 在 worst 档下是 noise。Improvement 太小，不值得 paper space。 在 reframed 单 claim 论文中完全删除。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 EC-HTE 本身优势微弱，adaptive allocation 在此基础上进一步优化的空间 很小。CATE-weighted vs uniform 仅 4% RMSE 改进和 11% bias 改进——统计上可能不 significant。原因：(1) 当 EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 本身就 modest 时，optimally allocating labels 的 marginal return 也 modest；(2) CATE heterogeneity 未知（需要 initial estimate），estimation error 吃掉了 allocation gain；(3) K=4 时 subgroup sizes unbalanced，minority subgroups 已经需要所有能得到的 labels，allocation 灵活性 有限。P2 priority 合理——这个实验在 worst 档下几乎无论文价值。\\n\"\n789\t  },\n790\t  {\n791\t    \"name\": \"Robustness to misspecified subgroup structure\",\n792\t    \"description\": \"EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义 noisy/misspecified 时的表现。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 对 misspecification 敏感。\\n\",\n793\t    \"results\": {\n794\t      \"noise_levels\": [\n795\t        0,\n796\t        0.1,\n797\t        0.25,\n798\t        0.5\n799\t      ],\n800\t      \"K2_ec_hte_rmse\": [\n801\t        0.16,\n802\t        0.17,\n803\t        0.19,\n804\t        0.22\n805\t      ],\n806\t      \"K2_global_rmse\": [\n807\t        0.12,\n808\t        0.12,\n809\t        0.12,\n810\t        0.12\n811\t      ],\n812\t      \"K4_ec_hte_rmse\": [\n813\t        0.2,\n814\t        0.22,\n815\t        0.26,\n816\t        0.3\n817\t      ],\n818\t      \"K4_global_rmse\": [\n819\t        0.14,\n820\t        0.14,\n821\t        0.14,\n822\t        0.14\n823\t      ],\n824\t      \"K2_ec_hte_coverage\": [\n825\t        0.93,\n826\t        0.91,\n827\t        0.88,\n828\t        0.86\n829\t      ],\n830\t      \"K4_ec_hte_coverage\": [\n831\t        0.92,\n832\t        0.89,\n833\t        0.85,\n834\t        0.82\n835\t      ],\n836\t      \"graceful_convergence_at_50pct\": false,\n837\t      \"ec_hte_worse_than_global_at_noise_25pct\": true\n838\t    },\n839\t    \"tables\": [\n840\t      {\n841\t        \"title\": \"Table 12: Robustness to subgroup misspecification (K=4, n_expert=250)\",\n842\t        \"columns\": [\n843\t          \"noise_level\",\n844\t          \"ec_hte_rmse\",\n845\t          \"global_rmse\",\n846\t          \"ec_hte_coverage\",\n847\t          \"penalty_ratio\"\n848\t        ],\n849\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n850\t          [\n851\t            0.0,\n852\t            0.2,\n853\t            0.14,\n854\t            0.92,\n855\t            1.43\n856\t          ],\n857\t          [\n858\t            0.1,\n859\t            0.22,\n860\t            0.14,\n861\t            0.89,\n862\t            1.57\n863\t          ],\n864\t          [\n865\t            0.25,\n866\t            0.26,\n867\t            0.14,\n868\t            0.85,\n869\t            1.86\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            0.5,\n873\t            0.3,\n874\t            0.14,\n875\t            0.82,\n876\t            2.14\n877\t          ]\n878\t        ]\n879\t      }\n880\t    ],\n881\t    \"figures\": [],\n882\t    \"analysis\": \"Robustness results 在 worst 档下是 EC-HTE 的又一 liability。Real-world subgroup definitions 不会是 noise-free，25% misspecification 是 conservative estimate。 EC-HTE 的 penalty ratio 从 1.43 增加到 2.14——比 clean 条件下更差。这进一步 限制了 EC-HTE 的 practical applicability。论文需要非常 honest 地报告这些结果 并明确 'EC-HTE requires well-defined subgroups' 作为 limitation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 coverage_ec_hte_small_n 在 [0.85, 0.92]。当 subgroup assignment 有 noise 时，per-subgroup CM 估计受污染，EC-HTE 的 stratification 变成 liability。 Global correction 对 subgroup noise immune（它本来就不 condition on subgroups）。 在 25% noise level，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 已经显著劣于 global（K=4: 0.26 vs 0.14）， coverage 跌到 0.85。HB shrinkage 理论上应该 gracefully degrade 但在 worst 档下 concentration prior 不够 strong 来 pull noisy subgroups back to global。这比 actual exp-010 结果（coverage 0.946 at 50% noise）显著差——worst 档假设 HB 实现或 prior calibration 有问题。审稿人会用这个结果论证 EC-HTE 在 real settings（subgroups never perfectly known）不可靠。\\n\"\n883\t  },\n884\t  {\n885\t    \"name\": \"Causal forest integration\",\n886\t    \"description\": \"CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction。Worst 档下 causal forest 放大了 debiasing-hurts effect（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更严重。\\n\",\n887\t    \"results\": {\n888\t      \"n_mc\": 100,\n889\t      \"n_configs\": 8,\n890\t      \"mean_abs_bias\": {\n891\t        \"naive_forest\": 0.16,\n892\t        \"global_forest\": 0.12,\n893\t        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.08\n894\t      },\n895\t      \"mean_rmse\": {\n896\t        \"naive_forest\": 0.18,\n897\t        \"global_forest\": 0.17,\n898\t        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.28\n899\t      },\n900\t      \"debiasing_hurts_cases\": 10,\n901\t      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\": 5.2,\n902\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global\": 1.65,\n903\t      \"ec_hte_forest_coverage\": 0.88,\n904\t      \"bias_reduction_factor\": 1.5\n905\t    },\n906\t    \"tables\": [\n907\t      {\n908\t        \"title\": \"Table 13: CausalForest results by K × regime\",\n909\t        \"columns\": [\n910\t          \"K\",\n911\t          \"regime\",\n912\t          \"method\",\n913\t          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n914\t          \"avg_rmse\",\n915\t          \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\"\n916\t        ],\n917\t        \"representative_rows\": [\n918\t          [\n919\t            2,\n920\t            \"extreme\",\n921\t            \"naive_forest\",\n922\t            0.14,\n923\t            0.17,\n924\t            \"—\"\n925\t          ],\n926\t          [\n927\t            2,\n928\t            \"extreme\",\n929\t            \"global_forest\",\n930\t            0.1,\n931\t            0.16,\n932\t            2.8\n933\t          ],\n934\t          [\n935\t            2,\n936\t            \"extreme\",\n937\t            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n938\t            0.05,\n939\t            0.24,\n940\t            \"—\"\n941\t          ],\n942\t          [\n943\t            4,\n944\t            \"extreme\",\n945\t            \"naive_forest\",\n946\t            0.18,\n947\t            0.2,\n948\t            \"—\"\n949\t          ],\n950\t          [\n951\t            4,\n952\t            \"extreme\",\n953\t            \"global_forest\",\n954\t            0.15,\n955\t            0.18,\n956\t            5.2\n957\t          ],\n958\t          [\n959\t            4,\n960\t            \"extreme\",\n961\t            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n962\t            0.09,\n963\t            0.32,\n964\t            \"—\"\n965\t          ]\n966\t        ]\n967\t      }\n968\t    ],\n969\t    \"figures\": [],\n970\t    \"analysis\": \"CausalForest 结果为 Claim 1 提供最强支持——5.2× amplification 是 dramatic 且 practically concerning。但 EC-HTE 的 RMSE penalty (1.65×) 和 undercoverage (0.88) 使得 'the fix is worse than the disease' argument 更 plausible。Worst 档叙事： 'We identify a severe bias mechanism (up to 5.2× with causal forests), but acknowledge that current correction methods trade bias for variance in ways that may not be practically acceptable.' 这支持 reframe 为 negative result paper。\\n\\nCausal forest 放大了 bias mechanism（max ratio 5.2×，因为 tree-based CATE 的 nonlinear estimation 在 subgroup boundaries 处 compounds error），强力支持 Claim 1。 但同时 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更重（1.65× vs global），因为 forest pseudo-outcomes 已经 noisy，再加上 per-subgroup CM correction noise 叠加。 Coverage 0.88 低于 nominal 95%——forest variance estimation 加 CM uncertainty 的 joint calibration 有问题。Bias reduction factor 1.5× 处于 worst 档上限—— EC-HTE 确实 helps on bias 但代价高。这进一步支持 'reframe around Claim 1' 叙事： CausalForest 使得 debiasing-hurts 更 dramatic（5.2× amplification），但 EC-HTE fix 的 cost 也更高。\\n\"\n971\t  }\n972\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5485ca2-d241-4783-8c96-df9835827383","uuid":"e8022ec6-0e81-46c2-9820-b97cbb421840","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:56:15.551Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE synthetic validation\",\n    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator vs MLE/Laplace，full regime sweep。 Worst 档下 HB 改进微弱，RMSE penalty 显著，partial pooling 在多数配置无实质优势。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.03,\n      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 110,\n      \"mcmc_divergent\": 0,\n      \"runtime_min\": 85,\n      \"total_mc_runs\": 3600,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50\": \"1-3%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100\": \"<1%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate\": \"2-4%\",\n      \"hb_coverage_min\": 0.85,\n      \"hb_coverage_median\": 0.9,\n      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup\": true,\n      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup_note\": \"Singularity guard triggers frequently (~15% of runs); residual instability even with 4-chain MCMC\",\n      \"hb_vs_global_rmse_median_penalty\": 1.5,\n      \"hb_beats_global_pct\": \"35% of configs (only extreme regime + n>=500)\",\n      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation\": \"8-12%\",\n      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_conclusion\": \"moderate sensitivity — k4 results shift meaningfully with scale\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE vs Global RMSE across regime × K × n_expert\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"regime\",\n          \"K\",\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"naive_rmse\",\n          \"global_rmse\",\n          \"mle_rmse\",\n          \"hb_rmse\",\n          \"hb_vs_global_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            2,\n            100,\n            0.18,\n            0.15,\n            0.17,\n            0.16,\n            \"+6.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            2,\n            500,\n            0.18,\n            0.15,\n            0.13,\n            0.13,\n            \"-13.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            4,\n            100,\n            0.2,\n            0.16,\n            0.25,\n            0.23,\n            \"+43.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            4,\n            500,\n            0.2,\n            0.16,\n            0.16,\n            0.15,\n            \"-6.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            2,\n            100,\n            0.14,\n            0.12,\n            0.13,\n            0.13,\n            \"+8.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            2,\n            500,\n            0.14,\n            0.12,\n            0.12,\n            0.12,\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            4,\n            100,\n            0.16,\n            0.13,\n            0.19,\n            0.18,\n            \"+38.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            4,\n            500,\n            0.16,\n            0.13,\n            0.14,\n            0.13,\n            \"0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"EC-HTE 在多数实际配置下 RMSE 劣于 global。Partial pooling 的 James-Stein 优势 被 per-subgroup CM 估计噪声淹没。仅在 extreme heterogeneity + n_expert >= 500 时 才有 RMSE 优势。这决定了 worst 档叙事：EC-HTE 不能作为 standalone contribution， 只能作为 conditional mitigation 附在 bias mechanism 主线之后。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设是 EC-HTE 优势微弱。HB partial pooling 在 moderate regime 几乎无 改进（heterogeneity 不足以让 stratification 获益），extreme regime 仅在 n_expert 足够大时才有意义。K=4 时 per-subgroup 样本太少（n_expert/4），CM 估计噪声高，HB shrinkage 不足以补偿。MCMC 收敛勉强合格但 ESS 偏低，说明后验几何复杂。Hyperprior sensitivity 在 K=4 时较高，因为 Dirichlet concentration 对稀疏子群影响大。整体结论： HB 是一个 marginal improvement over MLE，不构成独立贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Formal bias identity verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Bias = Δπ × Δτ product form 的 analytic derivation + MC 验证。Worst 档下 identity 本身成立（这是数学事实），但 amplification magnitude 处于范围低端。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r2_k2\": 0.99,\n      \"r2_k4\": 0.965,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.005,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.035,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 48,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_pct_note\": \"略低于 50%，因为 MC noise 在 boundary 附近导致一些 marginal cases 翻转\",\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k2\": 2.5,\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k4\": 2.4,\n      \"coverage_2se_k2\": 0.945,\n      \"coverage_2se_k4\": 0.93,\n      \"bias_amplification_median_across_configs\": 1.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: Bias amplification ratio across Δπ × Δτ grid (K=2)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"delta_pi\",\n          \"delta_tau\",\n          \"analytic_bias\",\n          \"mc_bias_mean\",\n          \"mc_bias_se\",\n          \"amplification_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            0.05,\n            0.1,\n            0.005,\n            0.006,\n            0.002,\n            1.1\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.2,\n            0.02,\n            0.021,\n            0.004,\n            1.4\n          ],\n          [\n            0.15,\n            0.3,\n            0.045,\n            0.046,\n            0.006,\n            1.8\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            0.5,\n            0.1,\n            0.098,\n            0.008,\n            2.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Debiasing-hurts breakdown by parameter region\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"region\",\n          \"n_settings\",\n          \"hurts_pct\",\n          \"max_ratio\",\n          \"median_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"extreme (Δπ>0.15, Δτ>0.3)\",\n            40,\n            85,\n            2.5,\n            1.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate (0.05<Δπ<0.15)\",\n            120,\n            52,\n            1.5,\n            1.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"low (Δπ<0.05)\",\n            100,\n            12,\n            1.05,\n            1.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bias identity 验证成功——这是 worst 档唯一完全 robust 的结果。但 amplification 幅度在 moderate regime 仅 1.1-1.5×，审稿人可能认为 'debiasing hurts by 10-50% is a known risk, not a new discovery'。Worst 档叙事必须强调 extreme regime 的 2.5× amplification 和 constructive example，同时承认 moderate regime 的 effect size 较小。 Carroll et al. (2006) 的 qualitative insight 已覆盖 'correction can amplify error' 的概念；我们的 quantitative product form 是增量贡献而非 breakthrough。\\n\\n\\nBias identity 是精确等式（population level），R² 接近 1.0 是数学保证，worst 档无法 改变这一点。但 worst 档体现在 amplification magnitude 偏低端：K=2 max 2.5×（而非 2.86×），K=4 max 2.4×（而非 2.41×）。这是因为 worst 档假设 moderate regime 占更多 权重——当 Δπ 和 Δτ 都不极端时，amplification 存在但不dramatic。Debiasing hurts 的 比例约 48%（接近 coin-flip），审稿人可能认为这不足以构成 'alarming finding'。K=4 的 R² 稍低反映了 sum-of-products form 在有限样本下的噪声放大。关键问题不在于 identity 是否成立（它一定成立），而在于 amplification 的实际幅度是否足以让审稿人认为这是 a problem worth solving。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Semi-synthetic benchmark (TweetEval sentiment)\",\n    \"description\": \"TweetEval sentiment 语料上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation，EC-HTE vs baselines。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 在 semi-synthetic 上优势微弱，RMSE penalty 大。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.08, S1=0.12, S2=0.14, S3=0.22\",\n      \"delta_pi\": 0.14,\n      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n      \"avg_abs_bias\": {\n        \"oracle\": 0.005,\n        \"naive\": 0.12,\n        \"global_corrected\": 0.09,\n        \"stratified_mle\": 0.07,\n        \"hb_ec_hte\": 0.065\n      },\n      \"avg_rmse\": {\n        \"oracle\": 0.04,\n        \"naive\": 0.15,\n        \"global_corrected\": 0.12,\n        \"stratified_mle\": 0.18,\n        \"hb_ec_hte\": 0.16\n      },\n      \"ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global\": 1.38,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global\": 1.33,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3\": \"-5% RMSE (HB slightly worse)\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n250_S3\": \"+8% RMSE (HB slightly better)\",\n      \"coverage_hb_overall\": 0.91,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_subgroups\": \"S0, S1 (low-error subgroups over-corrected)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: Semi-synthetic results by subgroup (n_expert=250, K=4)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"misclass_rate\",\n          \"naive_bias\",\n          \"global_bias\",\n          \"ec_hte_bias\",\n          \"ec_hte_rmse\",\n          \"global_rmse\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S0\",\n            0.08,\n            0.02,\n            0.07,\n            0.03,\n            0.14,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1\",\n            0.12,\n            0.05,\n            0.06,\n            0.04,\n            0.13,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2\",\n            0.14,\n            0.08,\n            0.04,\n            0.03,\n            0.15,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3\",\n            0.22,\n            0.15,\n            0.1,\n            0.06,\n            0.22,\n            0.16\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Bias-RMSE tradeoff summary across n_expert\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"ec_hte_wins_bias\",\n          \"ec_hte_wins_rmse\",\n          \"net_ambiguous\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            100,\n            \"3/4 subgroups\",\n            \"0/4 subgroups\",\n            \"4/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            250,\n            \"4/4 subgroups\",\n            \"1/4 subgroups\",\n            \"3/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"4/4 subgroups\",\n            \"2/4 subgroups\",\n            \"2/4\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 结果支持 Claim 1（debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 可见）但不支持 EC-HTE 作为 strong solution。Bias-RMSE tradeoff 在多数配置下 ambiguous——审稿人会引用 'reduces bias but increases MSE — net negative in practice'。Worst 档叙事：这些 结果 honestly show EC-HTE 的条件性优势，论文重心应放在 bias mechanism discovery 而非 EC-HTE method contribution。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global 在 [0.8, 1.5] 范围。这里取 1.38——EC-HTE 比 global 好 28% 在 bias 上，但 RMSE 代价 33%。Semi-synthetic 的 Δπ=0.14（moderate-to-high），足够让 bias mechanism 可见但不足以让 EC-HTE 在 RMSE 上胜出。HB 在 n=100 时对 minority subgroup S3 仍然 noisy（12.5 experts/subgroup for K=4），partial pooling 不够补偿。审稿人看到 bias 降了但 RMSE 升了，会问 'is this a net improvement?'——答案在 worst 档下是 ambiguous。Coverage 0.91 勉强 acceptable 但不 impressive。关键：debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 上仍然可见，这支持 Claim 1 叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Real-data case study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\",\n    \"description\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 比 global 差——real data 反向。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n      \"subgroups\": \"platform_group × text_length (4 groups)\",\n      \"delta_pi\": 0.1,\n      \"global_FPR\": 0.15,\n      \"global_FNR\": 0.55,\n      \"avg_abs_bias\": {\n        \"naive\": 0.22,\n        \"global\": 0.28,\n        \"ec_hte\": 0.32\n      },\n      \"ec_hte_minus_global_abs_bias\": 0.04,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_ec_hte_minus_global\": \"[-0.02, 0.10]\",\n      \"cate_direction_consistency\": \"2/4 subgroups consistent with domain knowledge\",\n      \"ec_hte_ci_width_median\": 0.35,\n      \"global_ci_width_median\": 0.22\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: Real-data CATE estimates by subgroup and method\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"misclass_rate\",\n          \"naive_cate\",\n          \"global_cate\",\n          \"ec_hte_cate\",\n          \"ec_hte_ci_width\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"plat0_long\",\n            624,\n            0.27,\n            0.15,\n            0.19,\n            0.22,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat0_short\",\n            624,\n            0.34,\n            0.08,\n            0.12,\n            0.09,\n            0.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat23_long\",\n            624,\n            0.3,\n            -0.05,\n            -0.08,\n            -0.12,\n            0.32\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat23_short\",\n            624,\n            0.38,\n            0.02,\n            0.05,\n            0.03,\n            0.36\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Real data 结果是 worst 档叙事的最大挑战。EC-HTE 不仅未改善，反而略差。但可以 salvage：(1) 没有 ground truth CATE，'worse' 仅指 point estimate 更极端 + wider CI； (2) Δπ=0.10 处于 diagnostic 的 'global suffices' 区域；(3) 高 FNR 是 dataset-specific limitation。论文可以诚实呈现为 'EC-HTE is not universally beneficial — consistent with our theoretical analysis showing conditional advantage'。但审稿人仍可能视为 disqualifying。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设之一：real data 持续显示 EC-HTE 比 global 差（|bias| 差距 ~0.04）。 原因是多方面的：(1) 高 FNR (~55%) 意味着 confusion matrix 接近 singular，逆矩阵 amplifies estimation noise；(2) 仅 2496 samples 分 4 subgroups，per-subgroup expert labels 不足（~600/group，但 CM 估计仍 noisy）；(3) text-feature subgroups 可能不对应 true misclassification heterogeneity structure（misspecified subgroups）； (4) Δπ=0.10 处于 moderate 范围，stratification 收益不足以补偿 variance cost。 Bootstrap CI 包含 0，说明差异 not significant——但 point estimate 方向一致地不利于 EC-HTE。审稿人会问 'if EC-HTE doesn't help on real data, what's the practical value?' Worst 档叙事：承认 real data limitation，frame as 'the diagnostic criterion correctly predicts this is a setting where global suffices (Δπ only 0.10)'——但这与 diagnostic CV AUC < 0.55 矛盾，所以叙事需要更 nuanced handling。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic criterion validation (CV)\",\n    \"description\": \"Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic 预测 global correction failure 的 ROC 分析。 Worst 档下 CV AUC 崩塌至 ~0.50，无预测力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"in_sample_auc\": 0.82,\n      \"cv_auc_leave_one_setting_out\": 0.52,\n      \"cv_auc_held_out\": 0.48,\n      \"subgroup_level_auc_cv\": 0.54,\n      \"setting_level_auc_cv\": 0.45,\n      \"correlation_product_vs_bias_amplification\": 0.4,\n      \"optimal_threshold_in_sample\": 0.025,\n      \"threshold_sensitivity\": \"AUC drops from 0.82 to 0.52 when evaluated out-of-sample\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Diagnostic ROC analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"evaluation\",\n          \"auc\",\n          \"95_ci\",\n          \"n_settings\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"in_sample\",\n            0.82,\n            \"[0.74, 0.90]\",\n            28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"leave_one_setting_out\",\n            0.52,\n            \"[0.38, 0.66]\",\n            28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"held_out_semi_synthetic\",\n            0.48,\n            \"[0.30, 0.66]\",\n            12\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic CV failure 是 worst 档的 defining feature。In-sample vs CV gap 巨大， 说明 Δπ×Δτ product 虽然在 population level 是精确 identity，但作为 finite-sample decision rule 不泛化。Worst 档叙事：放弃 diagnostic 作为 'decision tool'，重构为 'sufficient condition for concern'——当 Δπ×Δτ 非常大时，global correction 肯定有风险 （这是 identity 的直接推论），但 intermediate values 无法可靠区分。这实际上是从 Claim 3 退回到 Claim 1 的推论。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：diagnostic_auc_cv 在 [0.4, 0.55]。In-sample AUC 看起来不错 (~0.82），但 leave-one-setting-out CV 暴露了 overfitting：product Δπ×Δτ 的 threshold 在不同 DGP/配置间不 transferable。原因：(1) bias amplification 不仅取决于 Δπ×Δτ， 还取决于 n_expert, K, estimator type, subgroup size balance 等未建模因素；(2) 实验配置数量有限（~20-30 settings），leave-one-out 每次 test set 只有一个点； (3) product form 是 population-level identity，但 'when does it matter enough to switch methods' 是一个 decision problem，需要考虑 variance tradeoff，product form alone 不够。CV AUC ~0.50 意味着 diagnostic 本质上是 random guessing for new settings。 审稿人会直接否定 Claim 3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Expert label budget sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"n_expert × K × regime 的系统性 sweep，找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。 Worst 档下 crossover 要求大量 expert labels，moderate regime 永远不 cross。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mc\": 100,\n      \"grid\": \"n_expert=[50,100,250,500,1000,2000] × K=[2,4,8] × regime=[extreme,moderate]\",\n      \"crossover_hb_beats_global\": {\n        \"K2_extreme\": 500,\n        \"K2_moderate\": \"never\",\n        \"K4_extreme\": 2000,\n        \"K4_moderate\": \"never\",\n        \"K8_extreme\": \"never\",\n        \"K8_moderate\": \"never\"\n      },\n      \"hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_wins\": \"60%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_max_improvement\": \"+15% RMSE (K4/moderate/n50)\",\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median\": 1.6,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k4_n100\": 2.3,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k8_n100\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: RMSE crossover n_expert by K × regime\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"crossover_n\",\n          \"ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\",\n          \"global_rmse_at_crossover\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            500,\n            0.13,\n            0.132\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"never\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            2000,\n            0.088,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"never\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"never\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"never\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Budget analysis 彻底暴露 EC-HTE 的 practical limitation：在多数现实场景（moderate heterogeneity 或 K>4），global correction 始终是更好的选择。EC-HTE 唯一有价值的 scenario 是 extreme heterogeneity + small K + large expert budget——这是一个非常 narrow niche。论文必须 honestly present 这些 crossover，强化 'conditional advantage' framing。审稿人会用 K=8/never 结果论证 EC-HTE 缺乏 scalability。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median 在 [1.3, 2.5]，hb_crossover_k4_moderate = [2000, never]。Crossover points 全面上移：K=2/extreme 从 250 升到 500（需要 双倍 expert labels），K=4/extreme 从 1000 升到 2000（接近 impractical），K=4/moderate 和所有 K=8 配置永远不 cross。原因：worst 档下 EC-HTE 的 bias 优势本身较弱 （reduction factor 仅 0.8-1.5×），RMSE penalty 更重（per-subgroup CM estimation noise 高），两者叠加导致 crossover 需要更多 data 来 amortize variance cost。 K=8 是 worst 档新增的 stress test——8 subgroups 意味着 n_expert/8 极少，CM 估计 完全不可靠。审稿人会指出 'crossover requires 2000 expert labels for K=4 — at that point, why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?'\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL baseline comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"PPCI vs EC-HTE vs DSL 在四种 DGP 下的比较。Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A (covariate-only error) 也有 partial correction 能力，削弱 EC-HTE 独特性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_configs\": 48,\n      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n      \"dgp_a_covariate_only\": {\n        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.03,\n        \"ec_hte_avg_rmse\": 0.18,\n        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.08,\n        \"global_avg_rmse\": 0.12,\n        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.05,\n        \"ppci_avg_rmse\": 0.14,\n        \"dsl_per_subgroup_avg_bias\": 0.04,\n        \"dsl_per_subgroup_avg_rmse\": 0.2\n      },\n      \"dgp_b_outcome_only\": {\n        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.08,\n        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.02,\n        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.07\n      },\n      \"dgp_c_both_errors\": {\n        \"ec_hte_ppci_avg_bias\": 0.008,\n        \"ec_hte_avg_bias\": 0.15,\n        \"ppci_avg_bias\": 0.06,\n        \"global_avg_bias\": 0.12\n      },\n      \"dgp_d_no_error\": {\n        \"all_methods_bias\": \"<0.01\"\n      },\n      \"ec_hte_unique_advantage_over_ppci_dgp_a\": \"bias 0.03 vs 0.05 (40% better, but RMSE 29% worse)\",\n      \"ppci_partial_covariate_correction\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Method comparison across DGP types (n_expert=250, K=2, extreme)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"dgp\",\n          \"method\",\n          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n          \"avg_rmse\",\n          \"coverage\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"A\",\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            0.03,\n            0.18,\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            \"A\",\n            \"ppci\",\n            0.05,\n            0.14,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"A\",\n            \"dsl_subgroup\",\n            0.04,\n            0.2,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"A\",\n            \"global\",\n            0.08,\n            0.12,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B\",\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            0.08,\n            0.16,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B\",\n            \"ppci\",\n            0.02,\n            0.13,\n            0.94\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C\",\n            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n            0.008,\n            0.2,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C\",\n            \"ppci\",\n            0.06,\n            0.14,\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C\",\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            0.15,\n            0.19,\n            0.88\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 的 partial covariate correction 是 worst 档的关键 negative signal——如果一个 通用方法已经能 partially correct covariate error，EC-HTE 的 'structured correction for covariate error' 卖点被显著削弱。DSL per-subgroup 作为 simple baseline 表现 surprisingly close to EC-HTE，进一步降低 novelty argument。Composition 仍然 works but marginal gain over PPCI alone 有限。论文需要诚实承认 PPCI 的 partial coverage 并 reframe EC-HTE 的价值为 'structured + interpretable' 而非 'strictly necessary'。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A（纯 covariate error）也能 partially correct（bias 0.05 vs EC-HTE 0.03）——因为 PPCI rectifier 是 model-free，可以捕获任何 systematic error 包括 covariate-side。这削弱了 'EC-HTE is uniquely needed for covariate error' 的 论点。EC-HTE 仍然 slightly better on bias（0.03 vs 0.05），但 RMSE penalty 使得 net advantage ambiguous。DSL per-subgroup 的 bias 与 EC-HTE comparable（0.04 vs 0.03），验证了审稿人的担忧：'just apply DSL per subgroup, no need for HB'。DGP C 的 composition 仍然有效（ec_hte_ppci bias 0.008），但审稿人会指出 PPCI alone 已经 做到 0.06——composition 的 marginal gain 可能不值得复杂度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM annotator comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"多 LLM 比较 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。Worst 档下 heterogeneity 存在但 Δπ 较小，EC-HTE benefit 因此更弱。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_completed\": [\n        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n        \"gpt-4.1\",\n        \"gpt-4o\",\n        \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n        \"gpt-5.4\"\n      ],\n      \"effective_delta_pi\": {\n        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\": 0.15,\n        \"gpt-4-turbo\": 0.1,\n        \"gpt-4.1\": 0.06,\n        \"gpt-4o\": 0.05,\n        \"gpt-4o-mini\": 0.09,\n        \"gpt-5.4\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"all_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n      \"median_delta_pi\": 0.075,\n      \"ec_hte_benefit_prediction\": \"At median Δπ=0.075, expected bias amplification ~1.15× — minimal practical impact\",\n      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (4/6 models)\",\n      \"newer_models_lower_delta_pi\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Δπ by LLM model generation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"generation\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"delta_pi\",\n          \"predicted_max_amplification\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n            \"3.5\",\n            0.72,\n            0.15,\n            \"1.8×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n            \"4\",\n            0.81,\n            0.1,\n            \"1.4×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"4.1\",\n            0.86,\n            0.06,\n            \"1.15×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-5.4\",\n            \"5\",\n            0.9,\n            0.05,\n            \"1.10×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-LLM 结果是 double-edged：确认 heterogeneity 是 universal（所有 LLM 都有）， 但也确认它在 diminishing。审稿人可能用 GPT-5.4 的 Δπ=0.05 论证 'the problem is already mostly solved by better models'。论文可以 counter：(1) 即使 Δπ=0.05， 在 high-stakes CSS 中 any bias matters；(2) less-capable models 仍广泛使用 （cost reasons）；(3) Claim 1 的 formal characterization 不取决于 Δπ 大小。\\n\\n\\n所有 LLM 都展示 Δπ > 0.05（heterogeneity 是 structural），但 newer/better models （GPT-4o, GPT-5.4）的 Δπ 更低（~0.05）。这意味着随着 LLM 进步，misclassification heterogeneity 自然减小，EC-HTE 的 relevance 随之递减。Worst 档叙事：'EC-HTE solves a problem that is diminishing as LLMs improve'。Median Δπ=0.075 对应的 bias amplification 仅 ~1.15×——审稿人会问 'is 15% amplification worth the complexity of HB correction?'。论文可以 salvage by arguing that even 5% heterogeneity exists and Claim 1 formal characterization remains relevant——但 EC-HTE 的实际价值主张被 削弱。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Adaptive expert annotation allocation\",\n    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only。Worst 档下 adaptive allocation 的改进 negligible。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"allocation_strategies\": [\n        \"uniform\",\n        \"uncertainty_only\",\n        \"cate_weighted\",\n        \"oracle_allocation\"\n      ],\n      \"n_expert\": 250,\n      \"K\": 4,\n      \"regime\": \"extreme\",\n      \"avg_rmse\": {\n        \"uniform\": 0.175,\n        \"uncertainty_only\": 0.17,\n        \"cate_weighted\": 0.168,\n        \"oracle_allocation\": 0.155\n      },\n      \"avg_bias\": {\n        \"uniform\": 0.065,\n        \"uncertainty_only\": 0.06,\n        \"cate_weighted\": 0.058,\n        \"oracle_allocation\": 0.045\n      },\n      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse_improvement\": \"4%\",\n      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement\": \"11%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: Allocation strategy comparison (K=4, extreme, n=250)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"strategy\",\n          \"avg_bias\",\n          \"avg_rmse\",\n          \"worst_subgroup_rmse\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"uniform\",\n            0.065,\n            0.175,\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uncertainty_only\",\n            0.06,\n            0.17,\n            0.26\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cate_weighted\",\n            0.058,\n            0.168,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"oracle\",\n            0.045,\n            0.155,\n            0.2\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Adaptive allocation 在 worst 档下是 noise。Improvement 太小，不值得 paper space。 在 reframed 单 claim 论文中完全删除。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 EC-HTE 本身优势微弱，adaptive allocation 在此基础上进一步优化的空间 很小。CATE-weighted vs uniform 仅 4% RMSE 改进和 11% bias 改进——统计上可能不 significant。原因：(1) 当 EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 本身就 modest 时，optimally allocating labels 的 marginal return 也 modest；(2) CATE heterogeneity 未知（需要 initial estimate），estimation error 吃掉了 allocation gain；(3) K=4 时 subgroup sizes unbalanced，minority subgroups 已经需要所有能得到的 labels，allocation 灵活性 有限。P2 priority 合理——这个实验在 worst 档下几乎无论文价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Robustness to misspecified subgroup structure\",\n    \"description\": \"EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义 noisy/misspecified 时的表现。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 对 misspecification 敏感。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"noise_levels\": [\n        0,\n        0.1,\n        0.25,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"K2_ec_hte_rmse\": [\n        0.16,\n        0.17,\n        0.19,\n        0.22\n      ],\n      \"K2_global_rmse\": [\n        0.12,\n        0.12,\n        0.12,\n        0.12\n      ],\n      \"K4_ec_hte_rmse\": [\n        0.2,\n        0.22,\n        0.26,\n        0.3\n      ],\n      \"K4_global_rmse\": [\n        0.14,\n        0.14,\n        0.14,\n        0.14\n      ],\n      \"K2_ec_hte_coverage\": [\n        0.93,\n        0.91,\n        0.88,\n        0.86\n      ],\n      \"K4_ec_hte_coverage\": [\n        0.92,\n        0.89,\n        0.85,\n        0.82\n      ],\n      \"graceful_convergence_at_50pct\": false,\n      \"ec_hte_worse_than_global_at_noise_25pct\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: Robustness to subgroup misspecification (K=4, n_expert=250)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"noise_level\",\n          \"ec_hte_rmse\",\n          \"global_rmse\",\n          \"ec_hte_coverage\",\n          \"penalty_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            0.0,\n            0.2,\n            0.14,\n            0.92,\n            1.43\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.22,\n            0.14,\n            0.89,\n            1.57\n          ],\n          [\n            0.25,\n            0.26,\n            0.14,\n            0.85,\n            1.86\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            0.3,\n            0.14,\n            0.82,\n            2.14\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Robustness results 在 worst 档下是 EC-HTE 的又一 liability。Real-world subgroup definitions 不会是 noise-free，25% misspecification 是 conservative estimate。 EC-HTE 的 penalty ratio 从 1.43 增加到 2.14——比 clean 条件下更差。这进一步 限制了 EC-HTE 的 practical applicability。论文需要非常 honest 地报告这些结果 并明确 'EC-HTE requires well-defined subgroups' 作为 limitation。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档假设 coverage_ec_hte_small_n 在 [0.85, 0.92]。当 subgroup assignment 有 noise 时，per-subgroup CM 估计受污染，EC-HTE 的 stratification 变成 liability。 Global correction 对 subgroup noise immune（它本来就不 condition on subgroups）。 在 25% noise level，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 已经显著劣于 global（K=4: 0.26 vs 0.14）， coverage 跌到 0.85。HB shrinkage 理论上应该 gracefully degrade 但在 worst 档下 concentration prior 不够 strong 来 pull noisy subgroups back to global。这比 actual exp-010 结果（coverage 0.946 at 50% noise）显著差——worst 档假设 HB 实现或 prior calibration 有问题。审稿人会用这个结果论证 EC-HTE 在 real settings（subgroups never perfectly known）不可靠。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal forest integration\",\n    \"description\": \"CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction。Worst 档下 causal forest 放大了 debiasing-hurts effect（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更严重。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mc\": 100,\n      \"n_configs\": 8,\n      \"mean_abs_bias\": {\n        \"naive_forest\": 0.16,\n        \"global_forest\": 0.12,\n        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.08\n      },\n      \"mean_rmse\": {\n        \"naive_forest\": 0.18,\n        \"global_forest\": 0.17,\n        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.28\n      },\n      \"debiasing_hurts_cases\": 10,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\": 5.2,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global\": 1.65,\n      \"ec_hte_forest_coverage\": 0.88,\n      \"bias_reduction_factor\": 1.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: CausalForest results by K × regime\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"method\",\n          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n          \"avg_rmse\",\n          \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"representative_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"naive_forest\",\n            0.14,\n            0.17,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"global_forest\",\n            0.1,\n            0.16,\n            2.8\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n            0.05,\n            0.24,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"naive_forest\",\n            0.18,\n            0.2,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"global_forest\",\n            0.15,\n            0.18,\n            5.2\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n            0.09,\n            0.32,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CausalForest 结果为 Claim 1 提供最强支持——5.2× amplification 是 dramatic 且 practically concerning。但 EC-HTE 的 RMSE penalty (1.65×) 和 undercoverage (0.88) 使得 'the fix is worse than the disease' argument 更 plausible。Worst 档叙事： 'We identify a severe bias mechanism (up to 5.2× with causal forests), but acknowledge that current correction methods trade bias for variance in ways that may not be practically acceptable.' 这支持 reframe 为 negative result paper。\\n\\nCausal forest 放大了 bias mechanism（max ratio 5.2×，因为 tree-based CATE 的 nonlinear estimation 在 subgroup boundaries 处 compounds error），强力支持 Claim 1。 但同时 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更重（1.65× vs global），因为 forest pseudo-outcomes 已经 noisy，再加上 per-subgroup CM correction noise 叠加。 Coverage 0.88 低于 nominal 95%——forest variance estimation 加 CM uncertainty 的 joint calibration 有问题。Bias reduction factor 1.5× 处于 worst 档上限—— EC-HTE 确实 helps on bias 但代价高。这进一步支持 'reframe around Claim 1' 叙事： CausalForest 使得 debiasing-hurts 更 dramatic（5.2× amplification），但 EC-HTE fix 的 cost 也更高。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":972,"startLine":1,"totalLines":972}}}
