{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018ZuDTT4DF4DW8hX1W1VndC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me write the full paper. I need to:\n\n1. Single claim paper: \"Debiasing Can Hurt\"\n2. Cover all 9 experiments from experiment_data.json\n3. Honest about EC-HTE limitations\n4. Negative result + formal characterization framing\n5. EMNLP format, 8 pages main text\n\nLet me structure:\n\n- Abstract\n- Introduction (single claim focus)\n- Related Work\n- Formal Framework (Bias Identity - the core contribution)\n- EC-HTE as Conditional Mitigation\n\n\n- Experiments (covering all 9)\n- Discussion\n- Conclusion\n- Limitations\n\nI'll use ACL/EMNLP 2026 format. Now I'm mapping out the experimental results across nine different conditions—synthetic data with heterogeneous treatment effects, bias identity validation, semi-synthetic variations, real-world datasets, diagnostic tests, budget sensitivity analyses, baseline comparisons, multi-LLM evaluations, and adaptive allocation strategies—and organizing them into a coherent table structure that demonstrates the core finding across diverse settings.\n\nGiven the page constraints, I'll need to strategically place some results in the appendix while keeping the main narrative focused on the strongest evidence. Let me start drafting the paper using the standard ACL formatting guidelines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7305,"cache_read_input_tokens":38559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7305},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5485ca2-d241-4783-8c96-df9835827383","uuid":"8203f15c-6fe5-4443-81c8-cbb20745136e"}
